WEBVTT

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.180
There are a lot of openings
in the ground around here.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.270
They're all pretty deep.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.440
They're winding and connected.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.570
There are also some signs of life.
Like bats, of course.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.030
I think it's possible
we'll find water down here.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.900
<i>That bastard, Ango.</i>

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.700
<i>He's acting like nothing happened.</i>

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.330
<i>I'll never forgive him.</i>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.200
<i>Even if I stabbed him
in the back right now,</i>

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.830
<i>he would have no right to complain.</i>

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.040
<i>But I won't do that.</i>

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.250
<i>I'm just going to leave, anyway.</i>

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.840
<i>I'll help them find water first,
for the sake of Team Autumn.</i>

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.550
<i>Ms. Hana...</i>

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.560
END OF HEAT

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.690
Oh, there's a way up from here?

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.810
Yes, but it leads to a cliff.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.070
It would be hard to use it
as an access point.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.440
The pit I found is over here.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.570
It looks like it's about 17 or 18 meters
to the bottom.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.780
Maybe even more.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.410
All right, let's head down.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.200
Get ready, Hana.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.750
Depending on how things go,
we might be down there all night.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.640
Ango, you don't have to go down.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.850
Ryo, don't get the wrong idea.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.060
I can do this, no problem.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.190
I know, but you should
let me handle it this time.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.900
That's a relief.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.520
I'm also going to join you.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.480
The three of us will go together.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:19.740
Here, you can use this.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.070
Thanks.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.990
We'll use three anchors, just to be safe.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.790
That rock will do nicely.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.870
I guess we have to let them handle this.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.290
Oh, I almost forgot. Hey, Nijiko.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.250
I meant to ask you earlier.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.130
What did you mean by "reaper"?

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.380
We aren't sure ourselves.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.890
We just heard
the instructors talking about it.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:50.140
They said there should be a "reaper"
inserted into one of the teams.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.940
So presumably, whoever that is,

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:56.690
they must have come here
with orders to kill us.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.570
Maybe in the event that someone
posed a threat to the project's success.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.160
Or if we found ourselves in a hopeless
situation where we couldn't live,

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.500
they would kill us all
and commit suicide, I guess?

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.210
That's the conclusion we came to.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.290
That man... He might be the one.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.920
The "reaper" might be with Team Summer B?

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.680
Forget that "A" and "B" bullshit.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.760
We're the only Team Summer.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.060
Okay, I'm going first.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.270
Come down after me
when I give the signal, Hana.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:35.810
Did you hear me?

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.110
Yes.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:43.650
Ms. Hana, don't feel pressured to go
if you don't want to.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.200
Are you okay?

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.700
I'm fine. I'll go.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.910
Hana, I'll lend this to you.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.540
Take it with you.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.040
A flashlight?

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.790
It's an LED light you can charge by hand.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.210
We have no idea
what may happen down there.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.420
Well, no matter what,
it's best to just trust your instincts.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.970
Ms. Ran, thank you so much.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.100
Well, Ms. Hana, this is also for you.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.560
Some salt, nuts, and a first aid kit.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.150
Mr. Aramaki, I really appreciate--

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.110
Hana! Get down here!

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.610
Okay! Don't boss me around!

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:26.950
<i>I'm starting to tremble.</i>

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.910
<i>I'm afraid of going underground, but...</i>

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.370
<i>they gave me courage.</i>

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.790
Well, I'm off. I'll find water for us.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.540
The three of them
got to the bottom safely.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.340
We've still got some time before sunset.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.880
Shall we start a fire
and prepare something to eat?

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.390
I'll check out this opening.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.600
I can do it by myself.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.850
I would bet on him being the "reaper."

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.480
I see traces of water.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.770
Some must have run through here
during the rainy season.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.280
<i>Ryo is still mostly a stranger to me.</i>

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:07.820
<i>But considering what Ayu said...</i>

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.200
Ryo told me to stop you

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:14.240
because you couldn't keep yourself
from killing that girl.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:18.250
<i>I'm more worried about Ango
catching me by surprise than Ryo.</i>

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:23.420
Hana, shall I tell you a little bit
about Professor Takashi?

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:29.220
We first met Professor Takashi
when we were 13 years old.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.150
That's good. You've got it.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:43.440
Try to relax your shoulders more.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:46.900
And don't let your face get tense.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.740
Just relax.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:52.620
Let the wind carry the sound.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:59.000
I did it! I played all of "Tulip."

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.960
Playing instruments sure is fun.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:05.000
It's rare to meet someone
who has never played anything.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.130
Most people have played castanets
or a harmonica, or a recorder at least.

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.930
We were never taught to play the recorder.

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:17.560
And I've only seen tulips in pictures.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:19.850
That's also rare.

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.730
So how about we find some?

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.480
Koruri, listen.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:29.990
I'm going to leave
with Hana and the others.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:34.570
Hana and I don't want to deal with
that jerk, Ango, anymore.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.330
We also want to find
the other members of Team Spring.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:42.170
When?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:43.920
Sometime tonight.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.290
Please keep it a secret
from Ango and the rest.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.300
Let's go for a ride.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.340
What?

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:51.800
Come ride with me.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.180
-No, wait. The sun is about to set...
-It's fine. Don't worry.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.430
To be honest, I'm not really good
at doing anything athletic.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.270
No problem. Here, put this on.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:01.980
I've never done this before.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.100
That's okay, it's just like playing music.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.110
Come on, start running.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.480
Relax your shoulders.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.570
Make sure your face isn't tense.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.650
Just relax.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.240
Let the wind carry you.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.670
See? Just like playing music.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.210
The sun is going down.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.590
It's pitch-dark. The moon isn't even out.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:34.220
It's fine. Don't worry.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:37.640
I bet the view used to be
really beautiful here.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:39.390
Too bad.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:40.770
Just try and imagine it.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.770
Imagine what Hakodate used to look like.

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.770
Yes, it's stunning.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.730
A really breathtaking view.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.570
I've seen it in pictures before.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:52.780
Oh, a shooting star.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.110
It's pretty cute, for a meteorite.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:57.280
We should get back soon.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:59.080
Otherwise, they'll worry about us again.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.120
Koruri.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.000
Will you join us?

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:02.910
What?

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.710
I mean, will you leave with us?

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:10.420
Professor Takashi taught us
how to fight and use a knife.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:13.550
I would often get caught by
his surprise attacks.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.630
It was a test to see how I would react.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.140
Ango used to get attacked often, too.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:21.560
<i>I can't even imagine it.</i>

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:22.890
<i>My dad did that?</i>

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.940
He was fairly cool, refined,
and had a nice voice.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.020
I kind of liked him.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:35.820
Let's drop down and have a look.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.490
Hana, this time, you go first.
Can you handle that?

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:40.990
Yes, I can.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.000
Have you ever...

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.340
had to kill one of your own dogs before?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:58.890
I once killed a tiger
that I had raised since I was a child.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:05.350
It had contracted rabies,
and I just didn't want it to suffer.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:09.400
I have had a similar experience, yes.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:15.280
It had been severely injured,
and there was nothing else I could do.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.450
Do you regret your decision?

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:20.740
Do you believe that's what the dog wanted?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.580
I've never been sure, myself.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.790
Even now, I wonder
if I've made the right choice.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:32.000
The only thing I can say for certain

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.420
is that your tiger didn't resent you,

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:38.300
nor did it appreciate what you did.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:41.890
They simply don't think like that.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:46.980
And we can never be certain
of what they're actually thinking.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:50.850
That's why the only answer
we can find is in our own feelings.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:52.980
In our feelings?

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.440
Yes. In how much love we gave.

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:58.700
In how much consideration we gave.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:03.580
In how honest and straightforward we were
in dealing with them.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.910
<i>When that tiger looked at you
for the last time,</i>

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:13.290
<i>it must have felt happy,
even if only briefly.</i>

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.550
I have no doubt about that.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:20.550
Hana, how does it look down there?

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:23.140
There's nothing here.
It's just a flat drop.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.760
I can't see anything below.
I don't have enough rope to go further.

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.470
Is that so?

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:30.520
Ryo?

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:34.230
During the graduation exam,
I was attacked by Professor Takashi.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.730
We really went at it.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:39.650
I still have scars left from that fight.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:40.900
Ryo?

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:43.780
At that time, Professor Takashi told me
it was best to kill him.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.950
Otherwise, he would just attack me again.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.250
But I couldn't do it.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.870
And that cost Shigeru his life.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:54.830
Ryo! What are you doing?

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:00.260
Professor Takashi made me realize
that I should have killed him.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:04.430
He told me not to make
the same mistake in the future.

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:07.470
That's why I won't hesitate this time.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.430
Sorry.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.350
But I need you to die, Hana.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.400
Are you cutting the rope?

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.940
Your presence has made Ango
mentally unstable.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:19.610
You're causing trouble.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:22.610
But aren't you the one
who stopped Ango from killing me?

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.240
I won't let Ango kill anyone ever again.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.740
He'll fall apart, otherwise.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:31.370
But I can handle it just fine.
I consider it my duty.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.710
I'm not going to let Ango
kill either you or Haru.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:37.540
So it was you who tried to kill Haru, Ryo?

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.380
I couldn't let Ango do it.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.170
I won't let you hurt him anymore.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:51.310
Go and join Shigeru.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.390
Fall into that same darkness.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.560
Are you sure you're not the "reaper," Ryo?

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.230
I don't think it's wise
to thin our numbers so carelessly.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.780
Where are Hana and the others?

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.410
They haven't come back yet.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.080
Ms. Koruri? Is something wrong?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.410
What? No.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.420
Oh, they're back.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:19.420
Where is Ms. Hana?

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:20.920
She fell.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:24.420
The rope got cut on a rock,
and she fell into a deep crevice.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:26.930
There was nothing we could do.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:30.560
We tried to go and save her,
but the bedrock was unstable.

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:33.470
Neither our rope nor our light
could reach the bottom.

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:34.560
It's a real shame.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:39.310
Why the hell do you sound
so matter-of-fact about it, Ryo?

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:41.770
I'm going down there. Show me the way!

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.360
None of you are suited for this.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.200
I'm going to save her!

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:49.780
Nobody can be saved
after a fall from that height.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:50.780
She's already dead--

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:52.160
Try saying that again.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.460
Mr. Aramaki, let's go. I'll back you up.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.410
Gengoro...

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.670
Me too. I'll go and get Ban.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.590
Mr. Aramaki.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.090
Listen, Hana isn't the type
to just roll over and die.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:05.130
She's a fighter.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.180
<i>Calm down. You're still alive.</i>

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.060
<i>Looks like this is the only way out.</i>

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:25.110
This is the spot. She fell down there.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:28.650
Ms. Hana! Are you there?

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.950
Ms. Hana!

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:49.220
What should I do?
Which way do I go from here?

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:53.680
I'm all alone now.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:55.770
What should I do?

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:58.600
The sound of water?

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:01.400
There's water flowing somewhere.

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:03.690
I can hear it from below. Which means...

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:08.860
<i>I'm done being afraid.
I have a goal to reach now.</i>

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.370
Water is coming through the rocks.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:16.540
A river.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.120
Amazing!

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:22.500
Even in the dry season,
there's still all this water underground.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.550
<i>I survived, thanks to
Ms. Ran and Mr. Aramaki.</i>

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:36.720
The pull of the current looks strong.

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:39.310
It would all be over
if I got sucked down there.

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:42.940
Mind if I play "Goin' Home"?

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:44.020
Go ahead.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.980
<i>Hana can use this
to find her way back to us.</i>

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.390
What? I hear "Goin' Home" playing.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:21.730
Why? Where am I?

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.810
Does this mean the final test
isn't over yet?

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:26.310
Then where is Shigeru?

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.320
Shigeru!

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:32.990
If you're here, show yourself.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:36.740
<i>Shigeru isn't here.</i>

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:40.240
<i>You should know that,
you're the one who killed him.</i>

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:45.960
<i>Ryo may have cut the rope,
but you killed him just the same.</i>

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:49.090
No. It was the instructors.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:52.090
Professor Takashi planned the whole thing.
It's not my fault!

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:55.380
<i>If you were more reliable,
things would have been different.</i>

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:58.050
My leg was injured.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:00.010
I couldn't move as freely as I wanted.

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:03.560
<i>If you had trusted Shigeru,
you both would've made it out alive.</i>

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:10.530
<i>Your vanity, jealousy, and your need
to be the best are what killed Shigeru.</i>

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:13.320
No... You're wrong!

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.860
<i>It was all your fault.</i>

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.200
No. It wasn't my fault.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.580
There was nothing else I could have done.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.370
<i>Admit it. You made a mistake.</i>

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:28.790
<i>Admit it. You were a pathetic mess.</i>

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:30.880
<i>Apologize to Shigeru.</i>

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:32.840
<i>Apologize to Shigeru!</i>

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:38.010
No... It wasn't my fault.

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:42.520
<i>When did we take this picture?</i>

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.270
<i>I remember.
It was our last summer vacation.</i>

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:49.520
<i>We went on a trip to Sado together.
We took it there.</i>

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.150
<i>My dad said we were going to
visit someone who had helped him.</i>

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:59.780
<i>He took me to this big, old mansion,
and we met some old lady I didn't know.</i>

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:01.950
<i>And then...</i>

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:06.290
<i>If anything ever happens to us,
you should come back here.</i>

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:09.290
"If anything ever happens to us"?

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:14.050
<i>Didn't your parents tell you anything?
Like what to do in the future?</i>

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.300
Dad!

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:18.220
He was talking about
what I should do after I came here.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:22.100
What's that? I hear something.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:30.100
That's "Goin' Home."

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:32.650
Haru! Mr. Aramaki!

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:35.940
It's me, Hana! I'm down here!

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.360
They can't hear me.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:44.830
Go!

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:49.750
What's that?
It sounds like something flying.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:52.920
I've heard that sound before.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:56.340
It's a boomerang! Find it!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:01.050
Is this it?

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:04.760
Hana...

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.480
Something is carved in it.

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:09.480
"Water below"?

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.810
Hana. She even found water down there.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.230
I can't believe that idiot.

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:19.700
See? I told you. Hana is not the type
to just roll over and die.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:28.830
<i>I have no idea what this song is,
but they're sending me a message.</i>

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.250
<i>"Roger that!"</i>

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.170
<i>Water?</i>

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:36.630
<i>That's right, I came here to find water.</i>

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:40.010
<i>Things weren't supposed to
end up like this.</i>

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.130
Why did I come to the future?

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:43.840
What am I even doing?

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:45.350
What is my problem?

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:47.970
Hana...

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.100
Ango?

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:54.110
Stop. Don't come any closer.
Just back off!

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:55.900
Seriously, I'm warning you!

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:58.070
I don't want to be near you, anyway.

00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:00.070
What are you doing here?

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:01.650
Where are Ryo and the others?

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:02.910
You didn't see them?

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.740
I have no idea.
They went back up to where we started.

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:07.030
"Went back"?

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:10.040
Wait, you did something
to Ryo and the others, didn't you?

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.790
You left them to rot in this hole,
just like your father did.

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:14.040
That's what they did to me!

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:16.540
What the hell? Spill it!
Tell me what happened.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:17.750
I told you to back--

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:35.190
What is her problem? That moron.

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:37.480
Help! Somebody!

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:42.150
Mr. Aramaki! Haru!

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:43.110
It's Ms. Hana!

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.160
Hana? What? Where?

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:51.950
-Hana!
-Ms. Hana! I'm coming!

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.170
Let me go down first.

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:57.710
Hana, I'm on my way.
Just hang in there a while longer.

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:01.090
Haru, is Ryo over there with you?

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:02.380
No, he's not!

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:08.100
Haru, listen! Ryo is the one
who tried to kill you in that swamp.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:11.850
He tried to kill me, too!

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:15.190
He cut the rope and let me fall!

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:18.230
Be careful! Everyone, watch your backs!

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:20.520
Ryo did what?

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:21.860
I knew it.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.240
Roger that, Hana!

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:25.400
Don't talk anymore! Stay focused!

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:28.660
Koruri is on her way to you right now!

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:32.580
<i>I'm pathetic. A complete dolt.</i>

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:36.790
<i>I'm stuck here clinging to this rock
when I should have been by her side.</i>

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:42.170
<i>I had sensed that something was wrong.</i>

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.970
<i>But because she has a boyfriend,
I felt I had to keep my distance,</i>

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:49.180
<i>and this is the result.</i>

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:54.600
<i>Well, I'm through.</i>

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:57.060
<i>I'm not holding back
just so I can regret it later.</i>

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.230
<i>Once we save Ms. Hana,</i>

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:01.980
<i>I'm going to hold her tight
and not let go.</i>

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:06.610
Hana, hold on just a little longer.

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:09.450
I'll throw down the rope from up here!

00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:11.740
Ango?

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:12.830
Why...

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:14.540
Why aren't you helping her?

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:18.210
Hana! I'm going to throw the rope,
so grab on tight!

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:20.460
Koruri...

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:33.350
<i>Wait!</i>

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:36.100
<i>Don't go! Please don't go!</i>

00:22:36.180 --> 00:22:39.100
<i>Please don't leave me behind!</i>

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:40.060
Ms. Hana!

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:41.810
It's dangerous! Let me do it!

00:22:41.900 --> 00:22:43.940
When I yank on the rope twice,
pull me back up.

00:22:44.020 --> 00:22:45.230
Right.

00:22:47.860 --> 00:22:52.990
I can't even... go to rescue her...

00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:57.120
That's the sign!

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:05.550
The current is too strong.

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:07.340
Nobody could make it out of there alone.

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:11.890
The submerged part of the cave
continues on endlessly.

00:23:13.390 --> 00:23:16.270
I didn't see any sign of Ms. Hana.

00:23:18.060 --> 00:23:19.350
No way.

00:23:19.890 --> 00:23:22.230
She would never just roll over
and die like that.

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:25.020
I mean, she's always
so pushy and stubborn.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:27.480
<i>It should have been me.</i>

00:23:27.940 --> 00:23:31.030
<i>But I'm always such a damn coward.</i>

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.950
<i>I always survive
because I'm never the one to take action.</i>

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:47.880
Fubuki and the rest of my team
were killed by an animal.

00:23:49.720 --> 00:23:53.010
The animals here attack us
because that's how they stay alive.

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:56.470
But you, you're a human!
